  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Reading the Hidden Code\r\n\r\nEvery webpage is written in **HTML**. Before you inspect the otter site, here's the anatomy of an HTML **element**:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<h2>Cool Otter Facts!</h2>\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `<h2>` is the **opening tag**, `</h2>` is the matching **closing tag**, and everything between them is the **content**.\r\n- Opening tags can carry **attributes** - extra settings like `<img src=\"otter.jpg\">`.\r\n- Elements sit *inside* other elements. That nesting is the structure of the page.\r\n\r\n**CSS rules** control how elements *look*. A rule names its target (the **selector**), then lists properties: `h1 { color: navy; }`\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1. **Explore:** Hover over parts of the webpage and watch the **Tag Inspector** update on the right. It shows each element's tags, its nesting path, and the CSS rules that style it.\r\n2. **Find:** (a) an element with an **attribute**, (b) an element nested at least 3 levels deep, and (c) a CSS rule the element **inherits** from an element it sits inside.\r\n3. **Investigate:** Ask AI Tutor about one thing you found, for example:\r\n   - *\"Why does this paragraph get its font from `body`?\"*, OR\r\n   - Make a guess and ask, *\"Am I right that `</section>` marks where the section ends?\"*\r\n\r\nOnce AI Tutor explains your discovery, click **Continue**.",
