    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** This is the level where students learn to *read* HTML and CSS. The Tag Inspector shows, for any element they hover: its opening tag with attributes, its content, its closing tag (or a \"self-closing\" note), the nesting path down from `<html>`, and the CSS rules that style it - including rules inherited from ancestors, labeled with where they come from. The key insights: (1) every element is an opening tag + content + closing tag, (2) elements nest, and that nesting is the page's structure, (3) CSS rules name their targets with selectors, and some styles flow down from container elements.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"Pick an element. Where does it open and where does it close?\"\r\n- \"What's the nesting path of that heading? What is it inside of?\"\r\n- \"That paragraph's font - which element does the rule actually live on?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may hover quickly without reading what the Tag Inspector shows - encourage them to pause on one element and read all three sections before moving on\r\n- Students may think the closing tag is optional decoration - ask them what would happen if the browser didn't know where a section ends\r\n- Students may ask AI Tutor to make changes at this stage rather than just asking questions - redirect them: \"this level is about understanding what's there, not changing it yet\"\r\n",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "false"
  },
